## 5. Entity Scope

The entity list should be driven by SecureLogX production masking requirements.

Recommended core entities:

| Entity           | Description                  | Example                |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| `SSN`            | Social Security Number       | `123-45-6789`          |
| `EMAIL`          | Email address                | `john.doe@example.com` |
| `PHONE`          | Phone number                 | `704-555-1212`         |
| `FIRST_NAME`     | First name                   | `John`                 |
| `LAST_NAME`      | Last name                    | `Doe`                  |
| `FULL_NAME`      | Full person name             | `John Doe`             |
| `DOB`            | Date of birth                | `1985-04-12`           |
| `ADDRESS_LINE1`  | Street address line 1        | `123 Main Street`      |
| `ADDRESS_LINE2`  | Apartment/suite/unit         | `Apt 4B`               |
| `CITY`           | City                         | `Charlotte`            |
| `STATE`          | State                        | `NC`                   |
| `ZIP`            | ZIP code                     | `28202`                |
| `CREDIT_CARD`    | Card number                  | `4111111111111111`     |
| `CVV`            | Card security code           | `123`                  |
| `ACCOUNT_NUMBER` | Bank/account number          | `9876543210`           |
| `ROUTING_NUMBER` | Bank routing number          | `053000196`            |
| `NPI`            | National Provider Identifier | `1234567893`           |
| `MRN`            | Medical record number        | `MRN-778812`           |
| `POLICY_NUMBER`  | Insurance policy number      | `POL-12345`            |
| `DRIVER_LICENSE` | Driver license number        | `NC1234567`            |
| `PASSPORT`       | Passport number              | `A12345678`            |
| `IP_ADDRESS`     | IPv4 or IPv6 address         | `192.168.1.1`          |
| `TOKEN`          | API/session/access token     | `eyJhbGciOi...`        |
| `SECRET`         | Secret, key, credential      | `sk_live_...`          |

For the first production-focused model, do not try to support every possible sensitive entity. Start with the entities required by the SecureLogX masking policy and add more only when evaluation data exists.

