## 6. Standard JSONL Schema

The preferred labeled format is one JSON object per line.

### 6.1 Unlabeled Record Schema

```json
{
  "text": "Customer John Doe used SSN 123-45-6789.",
  "meta": {
    "source": "raw_log",
    "format": "text"
  }
}
```

### 6.2 Labeled Record Schema

```json
{
  "text": "Customer John Doe used SSN 123-45-6789.",
  "entities": [
    [9, 17, "FULL_NAME"],
    [27, 38, "SSN"]
  ],
  "meta": {
    "source": "manual_annotation",
    "format": "text"
  }
}
```

### 6.3 Required Rules

* `text` must contain the exact input string used for character offsets.
* `entities` must contain character offsets in `[start, end, label]` format.
* `start` is inclusive.
* `end` is exclusive.
* Entity spans must not overlap unless the training script explicitly supports nested entities.
* Labels must match `labels.json` exactly.
* Do not train from raw unlabeled text.

