## Step 4: Normalize Unlabeled Data

Script:

```text
scripts/normalize_unlabeled.py
```

Purpose:

* Convert plain text, JSON, XML, or mixed raw lines into a standard JSONL structure.
* Preserve source metadata.
* Make downstream scripts read a consistent format.

Expected command:

```bash
python scripts/normalize_unlabeled.py \
  --in data/raw/unlabeled.txt \
  --out data/to_annotate/pool.jsonl
```

Expected output line:

```json
{"text":"Customer name: Noor Chen","meta":{"format":"text","source":"unlabeled.txt"}}
```

Important rule:

Normalization does not create labels. It only converts raw data into a consistent structure.

---

## Step 5: Clean Logs to Message Text

Script:

```text
scripts/clean_logs_to_messages.py
```

Purpose:

* Remove log wrappers, timestamps, thread names, log levels, class names, and noisy prefixes.
* Extract the core message or payload.
* Improve model input consistency.

Expected command:

```bash
python scripts/clean_logs_to_messages.py \
  data/to_annotate/pool.jsonl \
  data/to_annotate/pool_norm.jsonl
```

Input example:

```text
2026-01-12 10:14:33 INFO [http-nio-8080] com.app.CustomerController - Customer John Doe used SSN 123-45-6789
```

Output example:

```json
{"text":"Customer John Doe used SSN 123-45-6789","meta":{"format":"text","cleaned":true}}
```

This step is useful for production-style logs because the NER model should focus on the sensitive payload, not the logging framework noise.

---

## Step 6: Active-Learning Sampling

Script:

```text
scripts/al_sampler.py
```

Purpose:

* Use the baseline model to score unlabeled records.
* Select records where the model is uncertain.
* Prioritize examples that are most useful for annotation.

Recommended command:

```bash
python scripts/al_sampler.py \
  -i data/to_annotate/pool_norm.jsonl \
  -o data/to_annotate/sample_for_label.jsonl \
  --model-dir models/pii_baseline \
  --limit 500 \
  --format auto \
  --dedupe \
  --seed 42 \
  --use-entropy
```

Fallback command when entropy produces too few samples:

```bash
python scripts/al_sampler.py \
  -i data/to_annotate/pool_norm.jsonl \
  -o data/to_annotate/sample_for_label.jsonl \
  --model-dir models/pii_baseline \
  --limit 500 \
  --format auto \
  --seed 42 \
  --fallback-unc-only \
  --unc 0.10 \
  --digit 0.00 \
  --min-chars 5
```

Important options:

| Option                | Meaning                                                                      |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `--limit 500`         | Select up to 500 records for annotation.                                     |
| `--dedupe`            | Remove near-duplicate examples before sampling.                              |
| `--use-entropy`       | Use entropy-based uncertainty scoring.                                       |
| `--fallback-unc-only` | Fall back to uncertainty scoring if entropy does not select enough examples. |
| `--unc 0.10`          | Minimum uncertainty threshold.                                               |
| `--min-chars 5`       | Ignore very short records.                                                   |

Expected output:

```text
data/to_annotate/sample_for_label.jsonl
```

---

## Step 7: Semi-Automatic Annotation

Script:

```text
scripts/annotate_pool.py
```

Purpose:

* Load sampled records.
* Run baseline model predictions.
* Show predicted entities to the annotator.
* Let the annotator accept, edit, add, delete, skip, or preview entities.
* Save confirmed labels.

CPU command:

```bash
python scripts/annotate_pool.py \
  data/to_annotate/sample_for_label.jsonl \
  data/to_annotate/labeled_pool.jsonl \
  models/pii_baseline \
  --limit 500 \
  --local-only
```

GPU command:

```bash
python scripts/annotate_pool.py \
  data/to_annotate/sample_for_label.jsonl \
  data/to_annotate/labeled_pool.jsonl \
  models/pii_baseline \
  --limit 500 \
  --local-only \
  --device cuda
```

Interactive controls:

| Key | Action                     |
| --- | -------------------------- |
| `a` | Accept predicted entities. |
| `s` | Skip record.               |
| `e` | Add or edit an entity.     |
| `d` | Delete an entity.          |
| `p` | Preview highlighted spans. |
| `q` | Quit and save progress.    |

Expected output:

```text
data/to_annotate/labeled_pool.jsonl
```

Annotation guidance:

* Skip noisy records that do not represent real SecureLogX input.
* Do not accept incorrect model predictions just to increase volume.
* Prioritize correctness over dataset size.
* Try to collect 50–100 high-quality examples per important entity type.
* Stop when new examples become repetitive or test F1 no longer improves.

