## Step 11: Evaluate Final Model

Script:

```text
scripts/eval_hf_charspan.py
```

Purpose:

* Evaluate the final model on the test set.
* Measure entity-level quality.
* Confirm whether the model is strong enough for ONNX export and Java runtime use.

Expected command:

```bash
python scripts/eval_hf_charspan.py \
  --model output_trf/model-best \
  --data data/split/test.jsonl
```

Recommended metrics:

| Metric              | Meaning                                             |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Precision           | How many predicted entities were correct.           |
| Recall              | How many true entities were detected.               |
| F1                  | Harmonic mean of precision and recall.              |
| Entity-level F1     | F1 measured per entity type.                        |
| Exact-span accuracy | Whether predicted offsets exactly match true spans. |

Minimum recommendation before export:

```text
Overall F1 >= 0.80
Critical entity F1 >= 0.85 where possible
No severe false-negative issue for SSN, DOB, CREDIT_CARD, CVV, NPI, TOKEN, or SECRET
```

For journal-ready reporting, capture:

* Number of train/dev/test records.
* Label distribution by entity type.
* Overall precision, recall, F1.
* Per-entity precision, recall, F1.
* Confusion/error examples.
* False positive and false negative analysis.
* Latency summary after ONNX export.

