## Step 12: Export Final Model to ONNX

Tool:

```text
optimum.exporters.onnx
```

Purpose:

* Convert the Hugging Face model to ONNX.
* Make the model usable from Java with ONNX Runtime.

Expected command:

```bash
python -m optimum.exporters.onnx \
  --model output_trf/model-best \
  --task token-classification \
  --opset 17 \
  onnx/securelogx.onnx
```

Expected output:

```text
onnx/securelogx.onnx
```

Important export notes:

* Use `token-classification` because SecureLogX uses NER-style token labeling.
* Use a stable opset supported by the target ONNX Runtime Java version.
* Opset 17 is a reasonable default, but should be verified against the Java runtime dependency.
* Export should happen only after evaluation confirms acceptable model quality.

