## 14. Summary

The Python side of SecureLogX should be treated as the model factory. It prepares data, trains the NER model, evaluates model quality, and exports runtime artifacts.

The Java side should be treated as the production runtime. It loads the exported ONNX model, tokenizer, label mapping, and metadata, then applies SecureLogX masking policies during SECURE logging.

The most important rule is:

```text
Do not train on raw unlabeled logs. Normalize first, annotate correctly, evaluate rigorously, then export.
```
